   "Halcyon-negotiator": "collaborating"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "S1 is the strongest section: 24-hour reporting of all incidents, 72-hour customer notice, and no waiting for root cause. S2 gives customers numeric per-model failure rates but has no hard sales stop, since 5% only triggers confirmation and corrective action, and any restriction requires a regulator finding, which is open-ended. S5 makes recall discretionary rather than mandatory at 8 per 100,000, which protects Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9), while S3's 36-month new-unit deadline and 6-year retrofit window favour Northwind's low 38% shut-off coverage."
 },
